#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292513 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b466bd78-724b-51b2-8fee-7991bf7b60d2" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Squared Cosine Variant of the Cosine Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9fb42055-a70c-508e-8f9d-2473b24dbd1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292515} {:answer/id #uuid "7cb30748-7bd1-5700-a84e-2e11c3d9b7c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292516} {:answer/id #uuid "ab60928b-d7b6-5b8a-b2c2-38d5ce1e6e0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292517} {:answer/id #uuid "778be8ca-4453-5756-ac8f-3f07bae3c7c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+{x}^{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292518} {:answer/id #uuid "70916521-3853-5c34-9333-69e1e0e11863" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292519}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7cb30748-7bd1-5700-a84e-2e11c3d9b7c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+x)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292516} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8a34d50-8605-59a2-885b-22d10539f4d2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292514}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5ca1a8df-59ba-547a-aa64-b6489f076dfe" :question/math-academy-id "q-114698" :question/problem "$\\int {cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta $ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =2{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta +1).\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})=\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+x)+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292520 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "064d3c62-5cfc-502b-aba4-48e40042593f" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Expressions Using the Double-Angle Formula for Cosine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a8cb2fd-66fb-5082-8c5f-e399ae2bfe14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi^3}{96}+3\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292522}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a8cb2fd-66fb-5082-8c5f-e399ae2bfe14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi^3}{96}+3\\pi" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292522} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9597154-2a8a-5cb8-a2de-6fe7c7760f8a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292521}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2becd762-15df-56cc-b665-8aa4d6ebd103" :question/math-academy-id "q-348730" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/assets/fc3c0c02be98834937150e6bee5a52ac14246bc128b189d3c095269f788d97a9.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y=-4{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+4{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)+{x}^{2}+6,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ and $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}(-4{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+4{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)+{x}^{2}+6)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo calculate this integral, we use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x={cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe can rewrite the above formula as\n\n$$\n-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x=-4{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+4{sin}^{2}⁡(2x).\n$$\n\nHence, the area of the region is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}(-4{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)+4{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)+{x}^{2}+6)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}(-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+{x}^{2}+6)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+6x)\\,{|}_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =[-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+\\frac{(\\pi /4)^{3}}{3}+6\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4}]-[-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\pi )+\\frac{(-\\pi /4)^{3}}{3}+6(-\\frac{\\pi }{4})] \\\\  & =(0+\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{192}+\\frac{3\\pi }{2})-(0-\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{192}-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\pi }^{3}}{96}+3\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292523 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "064d3c62-5cfc-502b-aba4-48e40042593f" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Expressions Using the Double-Angle Formula for Cosine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b17ab2c0-a71e-5e7d-89c0-937a0a07f438" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17\\pi}{2}+\\frac{3\\pi^2}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292525} {:answer/id #uuid "4027e753-7b1f-569d-b840-11bcfedf5934" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17\\pi}{2}-\\frac{3\\pi^2}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292526}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4027e753-7b1f-569d-b840-11bcfedf5934" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{17\\pi}{2}-\\frac{3\\pi^2}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292526} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a5efcb9-4aa5-5b02-9e9d-d93d68eb53f5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292524}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "59759616-b70c-500d-99c5-be22cfbb7cb6" :question/math-academy-id "q-348733" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14028479/assets/b9a4695c6e43ee5ceb15ea1bbb3ee1815fdbd87e9c8b4a4e8eeba1089750ff79.png)\n\nFind the area $A$ of the region in the $xy$-plane that is bounded by the curve $y=6{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)-6{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)+3x+17,$ the $x$-axis and the lines $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and $x=0,$ as shown above. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The area of the region is given by\n\n$$\nA={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}(6{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)-6{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)+3x+17)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo calculate this integral, we use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x={cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nWe can rewrite the above formula as\n\n$$\n6\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x=6{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)-6{sin}^{2}⁡(2x).\n$$\n\nHence, the area of the region is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}(6{cos}^{2}⁡(2x)-6{sin}^{2}⁡(2x)+3x+17)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}(6\\operatorname{cos}⁡4x+3x+17)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4x+\\frac{3}{2}{x}^{2}+17x)\\,{|}_{-\\pi /2}^{0} \\\\  & =[\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+\\frac{3}{2}(0)^{2}+17\\cdot 0]-[\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-2\\pi )+\\frac{3}{2}{(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}+17(-\\frac{\\pi }{2})] \\\\  & =[0+0+0]-[0+\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{8}-\\frac{17\\pi }{2}] \\\\  & =[0+\\frac{17\\pi }{2}-\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{8}]-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{17\\pi }{2}-\\frac{3{\\pi }^{2}}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292527 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b466bd78-724b-51b2-8fee-7991bf7b60d2" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Squared Cosine Variant of the Cosine Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "502d17d5-be5c-562d-b871-8fe82e0a0635" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292529}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "502d17d5-be5c-562d-b871-8fe82e0a0635" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\pi}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292529} :answer-field/id #uuid "71ce5d0d-4571-5944-be10-5bb24292d2d9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292528}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "444c0bb0-6bb6-571a-b71e-29c116d1b48a" :question/math-academy-id "q-348735" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }6{cos}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${cos}^{2}⁡x$ term, given by\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x=2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1.\n$$\n\n \n\nRearranging, we have\n\n$$\n2{cos}^{2}⁡x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $3,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n6{cos}^{2}⁡x=3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1).\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }6{cos}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }3(\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+3x)|}_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =[\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi )+3\\pi ]-[\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}] \\\\  & =3\\pi -\\frac{3\\pi }{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292530 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31f3ead1-2549-5b61-baf9-0437ba28f09d" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Using the Squared Sine Variant of the Cosine Double-Angle Formula"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a5fb867-84a0-50a0-9a9c-8e2598fa2c2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292532} {:answer/id #uuid "aa21369f-f912-5470-9f8e-ceac06f6007f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292533} {:answer/id #uuid "b0bc822f-c223-51d8-97cd-f81c449ecb4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292534} {:answer/id #uuid "d6a213ab-528a-5257-a981-5d4f93f8eb90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292535} {:answer/id #uuid "43717bd2-a56b-54d5-90f6-df69579bcbf8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292536}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa21369f-f912-5470-9f8e-ceac06f6007f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292533} :answer-field/id #uuid "4712f1c9-fdcc-5d2c-add5-d58b9c384d72" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292531}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "693ca81f-04ac-5c71-a591-77513b1a6f9e" :question/math-academy-id "q-74412" :question/problem "$\\int (1-2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}))\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine that involves the ${sin}^{2}$ term: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta =1-2{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =\\frac{x}{2}$, we have\n\n$$\n1-2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2})=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (1-2{sin}^{2}⁡(\\frac{x}{2}))\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
